# Secondary review — slice 0185, postmortem 01

This is the owning orchestrator's advisory review of the agent-written
[primary postmortem](0185-01.postmortem-md), for event
`b66b7530fd6b47ab8bb23069cf27802c`. Recommendations await operator agreement.
Only this report was written; no repair, gate run, commit or restart was performed.

## Cause

The blocker is an omitted test-fixture migration in step 0185's authorized
effects. Its selected UI tests include an accepted scene-save fact whose fixture
sets both a refusing storage proxy and `ReadOnlyKitAccess`. That fact expects the
storage failure prefix `Not saved to the kit — `.

Step 0185 intentionally adds an earlier UI-model guard. With read-only access,
`SceneSave` must return exactly `The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.`
without calling the proxy. Both messages cannot satisfy the existing fixture.
The step explicitly adapts the analogous `InverseConstructorTests` fixture, but
does not authorize adapting `SceneSaveLoadTests.fs`. The worker, judge and resolver
correctly identified the conflict and preserved the unauthorized file.

The smallest repair is to remove only `access = ReadOnlyKitAccess` from that
scene-save fixture. Its inherited access is read-write, because `openSceneKit`
opens it that way. Keeping `proxy = ordered.kit.proxy.readOnlyView` then makes
the test exercise a storage refusal after the UI-model guard allows the request.
Every assertion, test identity and case count remains unchanged. The newly
declared tests separately exercise genuine read-only model refusal and disabled
controls. This preserves the two distinct failure paths rather than deleting
coverage to obtain a pass.

This conclusion is established by source tracing, not a new test execution.
The actual repaired behavior must still be measured before declaring it green.

